  "Number": 4,
  "Question": "For all real numbers \\(x,\\) \\(x[x\\{x(2-x)-4\\}+10]+1\\) equals",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-x^4+2x^3+4x^2+10x+1\\)",
    "B": "\\(-x^4-2x^3+4x^2+10x+1\\)",
    "C": "\\(-x^4-2x^3-4x^2+10x+1\\)",
    "D": "\\(-x^4-2x^3-4x^2-10x+1\\)",
    "E": "\\(-x^4+2x^3-4x^2+10x+1\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "Work from the innermost parentheses outward, multiplying every term by each surrounding \\(x\\). First,\n\\[\nx(2-x)-4=-x^2+2x-4.\n\\]\nMultiplying this result by \\(x\\) and adding \\(10\\) gives\n\\[\nx(-x^2+2x-4)+10\n=-x^3+2x^2-4x+10.\n\\]\nFinally, multiply by the outer \\(x\\) and add \\(1\\):\n\\[\nx(-x^3+2x^2-4x+10)+1\n=-x^4+2x^3-4x^2+10x+1.\n\\]\nThus the expression equals \\(\\boxed{-x^4+2x^3-4x^2+10x+1}\\) for every real \\(x\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{E}}\\).",
